      "writtenOn": "2022-03-29T04:18:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this call will invoke a deferred function (5 ms) delay.\nThis is called on every new state, and a new request to schedule the function\nwill be ignore (the delay on the first request is honoured).\nMaybe you need k_work_reschedule instead. I don\u0027t quite understand the\nbackground here, so I can\u0027t claim to know what the right thing to do is.\nI do observe that the deferred function does check the state at the time it gets called, so maybe the deferred function only does something under certain circumstances, but it is being invokved every time the state changes.\nMaybe it should be more selective, and part of the state machine handling (i.e\nat the appropriate states, invoke the deferred function.",
      "revId": "e7393d743d110221fa499669e6f39ac4c362f663",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
